---
import SiteLayout from '@web/site/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Img from '@web/site/components/Img.astro';
import Icon from '@web/site/components/Icon';
import { href } from '@web/site/config';
import { timeline, values } from '@web/site/data';
---
<SiteLayout title="About Tilana van Tonder" current="about" description="Tilana's story: rebuilding after pregnancy, an honest relationship with food, and realistic strength for women and men.">
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="wrap about-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
        <h1 class="display display-sm">
          <span class="line"><span style="--i:0">Finding strength.</span></span>
          <span class="line"><span style="--i:1">Building</span></span>
          <span class="line"><span style="--i:2"><em>healthy habits.</em></span></span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lede" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.4">My own journey includes rebuilding after pregnancy, but this space is for women and men at every stage of life who want to move well, feel stronger, and create habits that last.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="about-portrait" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.2">
        <div class="frame"><Img name="tilana-portrait" alt="Tilana van Tonder smiling in a white shirt" sizes="(max-width: 52rem) 80vw, 22rem" priority /></div>
        <div class="sticker sticker-b tone-white">Former teacher.<br /><small>Runner. Mom. Still learning.</small></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="story-grid">
      <aside class="story-side" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why I started</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Strength that fits <em>real life.</em></h2>
        <div class="story-photos">
          <Img name="tilana-training" alt="Tilana van Tonder training on a gym mat" sizes="(max-width: 52rem) 70vw, 26rem" />
          <Img name="tilana-strength" alt="Tilana van Tonder strength training with dumbbells" sizes="(max-width: 52rem) 50vw, 18rem" />
        </div>
      </aside>
      <div class="story-copy" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.1">
        <p>Pregnancy and motherhood changed my time, my energy, and the way I related to my body. Rebuilding taught me that progress does not need to look dramatic to be meaningful.</p>
        <p>Those lessons reach far beyond pregnancy. Consistent movement, practical nourishment, and small promises kept over time can help anyone build a stronger, healthier foundation.</p>
        <p>This space is for women returning to movement before or after pregnancy, women who have not experienced pregnancy, and men who want a realistic approach to strength and lasting healthy habits - without pressure, perfection, or quick fixes.</p>
        <blockquote class="worth-quote card tone-terracotta">
          <p>Your size and your weight do <em>not</em> define your worth.</p>
          <span>There is no body you need to earn before you are allowed to feel strong, capable, and at home in yourself.</span>
        </blockquote>
        <p>I am also not perfect, and I will never pretend to be. If you are looking for a trainer with no cellulite and no stretch marks, I am not the person. I am real, raw, and honest - and I would rather show up that way than sell you an image that is not true.</p>
        <div class="honest-note card tone-sage">
          <strong>Honest boundaries</strong>
          <p>I am not a qualified coach (yet). What I share comes from years of personal experimentation, learning, and lived experience with strength, movement, nutrition, and healthy routines. It is general information, not medical or clinical advice. Pain, injury, pregnancy-related concerns, nutrition concerns, or other health issues should be discussed with an appropriately qualified doctor, physiotherapist, dietitian, or healthcare professional.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head split" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">My story so far</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Every season <em>taught me something.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <a class="link-arrow" href={href('/blog/welcome-a-little-about-me')}>Read my welcome letter <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <ol class="timeline">
        {timeline.map((t, i) => (
          <li data-reveal data-reveal-delay={String((i % 3) * 0.08)}>
            <span class="tl-n">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span class="tl-when">{t.when}</span>
            <strong>{t.title}</strong>
            <p>{t.copy}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">What matters here</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Kind, honest, <em>sustainable.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="values-grid">
      {values.map((v, i) => (
        <article class={`value-card card lift tone-${v.tone}`} data-reveal data-reveal-delay={String(i * 0.08)}>
          <span class="value-n">{v.n}</span>
          <h3>{v.title}</h3>
          <p>{v.copy}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band card tone-white" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="h2">Find the program that meets you <em>where you are.</em></h2>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={href('/program')}>Explore all programs <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
        <a class="btn" href={href('/contact')}>Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
